<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles II of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1630–1685</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> was king of England, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and Ireland, restored to the throne in 1660 after the Commonwealth. His marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-of-braganza">Catherine of Braganza</a> brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a> to England, and he granted charters for Carolina, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> and gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> to his brother James. Many English colonies of the later 17th century began with his grants.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-england.jpg" alt="Charles II of England" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Michael Wright · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Charles_II_by_John_Michael_Wright_or_studio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
